//     fail-closed (per probe output in the prior audit).

// Result: MIXED — constant-time holds; ML-KEM/ML-DSA lack
// on-disk KAT companions (the prior 2026-09-11 sweep did not catch
// this; **NEW finding**).

// ## 5. Boundary 4 — Process execution (PATH injection)

// Files: `oodar/fs/os/sys_exec_wait.c` (just fixed in prior turn,
// commit `6fe266c`, this session).

// Method: `grep "PATH" fs/os/sys_exec_wait.c` confirms the
// PATH-inherit pattern:
//   - `oo_env_matches_filter`: now also matches `PATH` (length 4).
//   - `oo_build_child_env`: tracks `path_inherited`; only emits
//     the hardcoded `PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin` fallback
//     when the parent had no PATH.
//
// Before the fix: every child inherited the hardcoded
// `/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin`, which opened a binary-shadow
// attack surface from `/usr/local/bin` (a privileged location the
// parent may not have trusted).
//
// After the fix: child inherits parent's PATH when set; fallback
// only on parent-PATH-empty.
//
// **Cross-ref**: 2026-09-11 focused-oodar.oot §5 item #5 from this
// session marked this fix as HIGH; this re-sweep confirms the fix
// landed and is correct.
//
// Remaining open (v4.2.0 follow-up, CHANGES.md): `app/xlang/xlang.c`
// and `app/xlang/ffi_sec.c` still use `oo_child_filter_env` which
// mutates global `environ`. Same root-cause family; out of scope
// for this audit round.

// Result: PASS — the M5 fix landed correctly. The
// `oo_child_filter_env` migration to localized env is documented
// as a v4.2.0 follow-up; no immediate vulnerability since the
// affected paths are `oo_lto_xlang_link` and the minisign invoker,
// both cap-gated and not exposed to user input.

